{'symbol': 'DUK', 'date': '2022-04-22 15:26:00', 'title': 'INDIANA FIRST LADY JANET HOLCOMB JOINS DUKE ENERGY VOLUNTEERS TO PLANT 5,000 TREES AT RAVINIA STATE FOREST', 'text': 'PLAINFIELD, IND. , APRIL 22, 2022 /PRNEWSWIRE/ -- INDIANA FIRST LADY JANET HOLCOMB, ALONG WITH INDIANA DEPARTMENT OF NATURAL RESOURCES (DNR) DIRECTOR DAN BORTNER AND INDIANA NATURAL RESOURCES FOUNDATION (INRF) EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR JODY KRESS, TODAY JOINED DUKE ENERGY INDIANA STATE PRESIDENT STAN PINEGAR AND COMPANY EMPLOYEES TO PLANT 5,000 TREES AT RAVINIA STATE FOREST IN MORGAN COUNTY.'}{'symbol': 'DUK', 'date': '2022-04-22 15:23:00', 'title': 'DUKE ENERGY CELEBRATES EARTH DAY WITH $100,000 IN GRANT FUNDING TO IMPROVE ACCESS TO SOUTH CAROLINA PARKS, TRAILS', 'text': '- FUNDING IS PART OF $400,000 MONTHLONG CAMPAIGN FOCUSED ON SUSTAINABILITY, ENVIRONMENTAL EFFORTS ACROSS PALMETTO STATE.\xa0 - GRANTS WILL SUPPORT PROJECTS BY SOUTH CAROLINA STATE PARKS, THE NATURE CONSERVANCY, PALMETTO TRAIL AND FOOTHILLS TRAIL.'}{'symbol': 'DUK', 'date': '2022-04-22 14:54:00', 'title': "MAJOR MILESTONES DRIVE DUKE ENERGY FLORIDA'S COMMITMENT TO A CLEANER, SMARTER ENERGY FUTURE JUST IN TIME FOR EARTH DAY", 'text': 'STATEWIDE $2 BILLION SOLAR INVESTMENT. THREE OF SIX ENERGY STORAGE SITES COMPLETED.'}